 and  talk to nevadans because that's what  initiative's supposed to do and then if  they say that sounds good to me they  sign we turned in  266 000 signatures so when we were  talking to people and gave them the  explanation i just gave you they said  let me sign that so we know we already  have a lot of support  the problem is is that the democratic  party sued us in court because they  didn't want to change things and  political parties like the status quo  and so that's not surprising to us the  nevada supreme court ruled in our favor  now what we need to do is do exactly  what i'm doing right now is get the word  out we prevailed we had enough  signatures you know we're going to be on  the ballot in november we need people to  vote yes  is there a benefit to going i'm not  saying it's exactly the same i  acknowledge that right but just having  more people involved in the electoral  process for longer beyond the price yes  yes we want and our turnout for this  primary in clark county was 23 percent  that's not consensus we want more people  being engaged so we're we're looking at  again different countries that use this  process alaska is using it right now  maine has been using it they do have  more people showing up because now my  candidate made it through because what  we we see is that if your candidate  doesn't make it through the primary  you're like well i didn't like those two  what do i care now if your candidate  made it through you're more likely to be  engaged and candidates are more likely  to say all right i was number five i'm  probably not going to win i know you're  number one  i have voters that really like me if you  would maybe take one of my ideas i could  tell my voters to make you their number  two but isn't the whole idea of the  primary to  sort of  sort that out so that at the general  election you have you can at the end of  the day find consensus versus keeping a  whole bunch of candidates strung along  through until the general election  so a lot of people will tell you the  purpose of a primary is to pick the  nominees for the political parties that  is not true  if you again the nonpartisan races  if somebody gets 50 plus one in the  nonpartisan race they just got elected  we now have a new sheriff right right so  we're not using the primaries for that  but even in the partisan races there was  a law passed in 2015 it's sb 499 and it  says if only one party  fields candidates in a partisan election  whoever wins in that closed primary is  the candidate  and so we are electing people even in  the closed primary and so what we're  saying is is we think the political  parties are controlling the primary too  much  and we want to have more people being  able to participate we want more  candidates to also go forward because  two you know we've got 1.7 million  voters in clark county two people are  actually going to represent that we  don't think so  if you want to know more about the  initiative it's a lot to digest we can  watch the full interview there on  8newsnow.com
 

